this is a bad entry point because it relies on lua where it need not to. Instead:

- make a custom event class
- store a list of arg types expected (std::type_index)
- register on the eventBus
- have Lua pick it up and parse called invocations. You can pass arguments as a vector<variant<...>> and do `using` for the variant<> of allowed types - int, double, window, layer, whatever.
- eventBus can reject invocations with invalid args based on the typeinfo

```cpp
class CCustomEvent {
   public:
    using ValidVariant = std::variant<int, double, PHLWINDOWREF, ...>;
     CCustomEvent(std::vector<const std::type_index*> expected);

     void emit(std::vector<ValidVariant>&& data); // does type-checking
};
```

